  "details": "1. Added a VRC Parent Constraint to my avatar.\n\n2. Added one Source and pressed \"Activate\".\n\n3. Target transform moves/rotates.\n\nExpected behavior: \"Activate\" is supposed to set appropriate offsets so that the current transform is retained (does not move or rotate).\n\nI assume the calculation for the offsets has something wrong with it. It almost looks like its not calculating rotation offsets at all (the rotation offsets remain zero) though the position moves incorrectly as well. Performing the same steps with a classic Parent Constraint behaves as expected.",
